Fixed the content-type colours doing nothing when set from the themes control panel. `_root.scss` read `--event-color-override`, `--file-color-override` and `--image-color-override`, which nothing writes: a theme's `event_color_light` setting reaches the page as `--event-color-light`. The three tokens now read the properties a theme actually sets, through `light-dark()` like every other colour, so they follow the colour mode as well. The contract between the backend schema and the stylesheet is now tested from both ends — the previous tests checked that a field derives a custom property, but not that any stylesheet reads it. @ericof
